-- The language a player's client reads (playerbot_language.h, 28 September).
--
-- The server cannot see a client's language switch, and what it says to one
-- player - the companion's lines, a war's or a duel's refusal, our quests'
-- dialogs, the bots' notices - it says in one language. So at every entry
-- into the game (a login, a warp) it asks: "PlayerBotLanguage" is a command
-- the client runs, and a client that knows it answers "/playerbot_lang en"
-- for any language but Polish, or "pl" (playerbot_lang.py). The server keeps
-- the answer as this quest's own flag, "en" - 1 for English - so it is there
-- at the next login before the question comes again, and every quest of ours
-- reads it as pc.getf("playerbot_lang", "en").
--
-- A client that does not know the question writes an unknown server command
-- to its syserr.txt and says nothing, and its player reads Polish, as before.
-- A bot has no client: the command goes nowhere.
quest playerbot_lang begin
	state start begin
		when login begin
			cmdchat("PlayerBotLanguage")
		end
	end
end
